# Line endings are fixed by the repository, not by each contributor's
# `core.autocrlf`. `rustfmt.toml` sets `newline_style = "Unix"`, so every text
# file must be LF on every platform or `cargo fmt --check` fails on a Windows
# checkout while passing on Linux.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide text vs binary by content, so images, archives and
# other binaries are untouched. Files that genuinely need CRLF say so.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
